},{"label":"Not diluting shareholders","ok":true,"evidence":"Diluted share count -2.1% YoY"},{"label":"Analyst estimates moving higher","ok":null,"evidence":"Estimate-revision feed not connected (Phase 2)"},{"label":"Management guidance increasing","ok":null,"evidence":"Earnings Intelligence Engine not built (Phase 2)"}],"thesis":"Apple (AAPL) screens at opportunity 66.0 with an expectations gap of 7.0. Reality 67.0 reflects +14.2% TTM revenue growth, +33.2% operating margin and +111.5% ROIC; pricing 60.0 reflects a fair multiple and strong price momentum. Primary theme exposure: Edge AI (trend 61.0). Macro fit for Technology in a Goldilocks regime is 53.0/100.","market_expectation":{"summary":"Priced roughly in line with its own history and peers; the market expects the current trajectory to continue.","evidence":["EV/Sales 10.6x (86.0th pct of own 5y range)","P/E 38x (43.0th pct of own history)","FCF yield 2.8%","PEG 1.2","12m return +32%, -1% from 52w high"]},"what_market_misses":["Operating leverage is showing up in margins faster than in the valuation."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (roughly 90 days after the last filing on 2026-07-31)","Edge AI: evidence that 'Power-efficient silicon, on-device memory' is easing via NPUs in phones/PCs/cars, low-power memory","Continued rotation into Technology"],"risks":["No engine-flagged risks; standard execution and macro risk apply."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 9% (currently 14.2%)","ROIC falls below 84% (currently 111.5%)","Operating margin compresses more than 200 bps YoY (currently 33.2%)","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +73)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","Edge AI theme trend drops below 45"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":0.0924,"current":0.1424},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":0.8363,"current":1.1151},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":0.013065773311612072},{"id":"rotation","label":"Technology rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-20,"consecutive":2,"current":73.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":48.599999999999994},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":17.4},{"id":"theme","label":"Edge AI theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"edge-ai","op":"<","threshold":45,"current":61.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"edge-ai","theme":"Edge AI","weight":0.3,"order":1,"effective":0.3}],"llm":{"thesis":"Apple is compounding at a rate its own history says is unusual: TTM revenue +14.2% and accelerating off a $466.8B base, operating margin 33.2% (+131bps YoY), FCF +42.1% to $136.7B, and a fortress balance sheet (net debt/EBITDA 0.12) funding $82.2B of buybacks that shrank the diluted share count 2.1%. The valuation tension is that EV/Sales sits at the 86th percentile of its 5y range while P/E sits at the 43rd \u2014 the same fact viewed two ways, and the reconciliation is margin expansion: the market is paying more per dollar of revenue precisely because each dollar now carries more profit. That means the bear case is not 'the multiple is stretched' but 'margins mean-revert'; if the +131bps of operating leverage and 29.3% FCF margin prove structural rather than cyclical, a 38x P/E against 32% EPS growth (PEG 1.19) is not demanding. The engine's 7-point expectations gap (reality 67 vs pricing 60) is modest and the stock is 0.9% from its 52-week high with a +73 Technology rotation score, so this is a trend-continuation/quality-compounder setup, not a mispricing \u2014 position size accordingly.","fundamental_read":"Growth is accelerating (+14.2% vs +12.8% prior) while margins expand simultaneously, which is the rarer combination and the reason net income (+29.9%) and EPS (+32.2%) outrun revenue by more than 2x. Cash generation is exceptional: $146.7B OCF on only $10.0B capex gives 1.06x FCF conversion and a 29.3% FCF margin, and essentially all of it is returned ($82.2B buybacks + $15.6B dividends vs $136.7B FCF). ROIC of 111.5% is structural, but incremental ROIC of 80.8% is meaningfully below the base \u2014 new capital is still spectacular but dilutive to the average, which is why the engine failed the 'ROIC expanding' check. Balance sheet risk is effectively nil at 0.12x net debt/EBITDA with $62.4B cash.","technical_read":"Unambiguous uptrend: close 337.02 above SMA20 (326.95), SMA50 (321.51) and SMA200 (287.16), with a 50>200 configuration and price 17.4% above the 200-day. RSI 62.9 and positive MACD histogram (1.20) confirm momentum without a blow-off reading, and the stock is only 0.9% from its 52-week high after +33.9% in six months. The 17.4% extension above the 200-day is the main vulnerability \u2014 a mean-reversion pullback toward SMA50 (~321) would be routine, not thesis-breaking; the engine's break level is a close >10% below the 200-day.","market_expectation":"At 38x earnings, 10.6x EV/Sales, 29.4x EV/EBITDA and a 2.8% FCF yield, the market is underwriting continuation: mid-teens revenue growth, sustained ~33% operating margins, and ongoing ~2% annual share shrink, with no multiple expansion required to generate equity-like returns. P/E at the 43rd percentile of its own history versus EV/Sales at the 86th says the market believes the higher margin structure is real and is capitalizing it at a normal earnings multiple. Momentum at the 52-week high plus a +73 sector rotation score means positioning is with the trade, not against it \u2014 expectations are 'high but not euphoric'.","what_market_misses":["The EV/Sales-vs-P/E percentile split is the whole argument: at 86th-percentile sales multiple but 43rd-percentile earnings multiple, the market has already validated current margins but is not paying for further operating leverage. Another 100-150bps of margin would flow almost entirely to earnings with no rerating needed.","Operating leverage is showing up in margins faster than in the multiple \u2014 33.2% operating margin with +131bps YoY and a 1.06x FCF conversion means reported earnings quality is improving alongside the growth, which historically supports multiple persistence rather than compression.","Capital intensity is the underappreciated asset: $10.0B capex on $466.8B revenue (~2.2%) means Apple participates in the AI cycle without the balance-sheet drag borne by hyperscalers \u2014 its FCF yield of 2.8% is unlevered by a capex supercycle.","The shareholder yield of ~2.0% (1.67% buyback + 0.32% dividend) is a mechanical EPS tailwind of roughly 2 points per year that compounds independently of unit demand.","Incremental ROIC of 80.8% versus a 111.5% base is a quiet signal that the marginal dollar is earning less than the average \u2014 the return profile is drifting down even as absolute returns stay extraordinary."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (~90 days after the 2026-07-31 filing): confirmation that +14.2% revenue growth and the +131bps margin trend persist rather than fade","Evidence that the Edge AI constraint \u2014 power-efficient silicon and on-device memory \u2014 is easing via NPUs in phones/PCs, which would extend the device replacement cycle driving current revenue acceleration","Continued capital rotation into Technology (+73 rotation score, the only sector above +10 in the entire table)","Further buyback authorization, given $136.7B FCF against $82.2B of repurchases and $62.4B cash"],"risks":["EV/Sales at the 86th percentile of its 5y range leaves no cushion if revenue growth decelerates back toward the high single digits \u2014 the sales multiple would compress even if earnings hold.","Margin mean reversion is the single largest earnings risk: EPS grew 32.2% on 14.2% revenue growth, so a large share of the earnings growth is margin-driven and therefore non-repeatable.","Price sits 17.4% above the 200-day and 0.9% from the 52-week high with RSI 63 \u2014 a crowded, well-owned trade where a macro shock produces outsized drawdown.","Regime is genuinely unresolved: Goldilocks 26.3% versus Stagflation 23.7% and Contraction 24.9% is near-uniform, and macro fit for Technology is only 53/100 \u2014 the sector rotation tailwind rests on an unstable base.","Coverage is only 0.75: estimate revisions, management guidance, narrative acceleration and insider/institutional flow are all unmeasured, so the thesis is blind to the exact channels through which sentiment usually turns first.","Consumer electronics demand is cyclical and a 14.2% growth rate on a $467B base is historically anomalous for Apple \u2014 some of it may be replacement-cycle pull-forward rather than a new run rate. (inference, not measured)"],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 9% (currently 14.2%)","Operating margin compresses more than 200bps YoY from 33.2%","ROIC falls below 84% (currently 111.5%), or incremental ROIC drops below ~50% signalling deteriorating capital deployment","FCF margin falls below ~24% or FCF conversion drops meaningfully below 1.0x, indicating working-capital or capex-driven cash erosion","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive readings (currently +73)","Combined Stagflation + Contraction regime probability exceeds 55% (currently 48.6%)","Price closes more than 10% below the 200-day (~258) with negative relative strength","Edge AI theme trend drops below 45 (currently 61.0)","Buyback pace slows materially such that diluted share count stops shrinking"],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Low-power memory suppliers (LPDDR/on-device DRAM and NAND): the stated Edge AI constraint is 'power-efficient silicon, on-device memory' \u2014 larger on-device models mechanically raise memory content per handset, and memory vendors capture that with pricing power Apple cannot fully negotiate away.","Leading-edge foundry and advanced packaging: Apple's fabless model means every node transition required to hit power-per-inference targets converts Apple R&D ($42.9B TTM) into someone else's wafer and packaging revenue.","Semiconductor IP and EDA vendors: NPU architecture licensing and design-tool intensity scale with the number of custom silicon variants Apple ships across phone, PC and wearables.","Thermal management, power-delivery and RF component suppliers: sustained on-device inference raises sustained power draw in a fixed enclosure, a physical constraint that must be solved with components rather than software.","Cloud inference providers and partner model vendors: Apple's ~2.2% capex/revenue discipline implies workloads too large for the device get offloaded, monetizing the constraint for whoever hosts them. (speculative)"],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"TTM revenue was $466.8B, growing +14.2% versus +12.8% the prior quarter","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Operating margin is 33.2%, up 131bps YoY; FCF is $136.7B at a 29.3% margin with 1.06x conversion","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"ROIC is 111.5% but incremental ROIC is 80.8%; net debt/EBITDA is 0.12x; diluted shares fell 2.1% YoY on $82.2B of buybacks","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"P/E is 38.1x (43rd percentile of 5y history), EV/Sales 10.6x (86th percentile), FCF yield 2.8%, PEG 1.19","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Price is 337.02, above the 20/50/200-day averages, 17.4% above the 200-day, 0.9% from the 52-week high, RSI 62.9, MACD histogram +1.20","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Regime is labelled Goldilocks at only 26.3% probability with Stagflation and Contraction together at 48.6%; Technology rotation score is +73, the highest of any sector","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"The market expects the current trajectory of mid-teens growth and ~33% margins to continue, with no multiple expansion assumed","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"The gap between an 86th-percentile EV/Sales and a 43rd-percentile P/E is explained by margin expansion, meaning the market has capitalized current margins but not future operating leverage","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"The ~2.0% shareholder yield provides a roughly 2-point mechanical annual EPS tailwind independent of demand","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Incremental ROIC of 80.8% below the 111.5% base signals the marginal deployed dollar earns less than the existing asset base","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Capex at ~2.2% of revenue lets Apple participate in the AI cycle without hyperscaler-style balance sheet strain","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Part of the 14.2% revenue growth may be replacement-cycle pull-forward rather than a sustainable run rate","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Easing of the on-device memory and power-efficient silicon constraint would extend the device upgrade cycle and sustain revenue acceleration","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Low-power memory, advanced packaging and NPU IP vendors capture disproportionate economics from Apple's Edge AI constraint","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Estimate revisions, management guidance and insider/institutional flow are unmeasured (coverage 0.75), leaving the thesis blind to early sentiment inflection","kind":"observed_fact"}],"confidence":0.58}},"technical":{"score":100,"passes":8,"criteria":{"above_150_200":true,"150_above_200":true,"200_rising_1m":true,"50_above_150_200":true,"above_50":true,"25pct_above_52w_low":true,"within_25pct_of_52w_high":true,"rs_positive_6m":true},"ready":true,"stage":"stage2_uptrend","close":337.02,"sma50":321.51,"sma1